WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.700
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.540
It's been 73 hours since the Astronaut
Training Center Liebe Delta was crushed.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.170
487 survivors escaped to
the Training Ship Liebel...

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.810
...and there, learned of
the Spaceship Ryvius.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:20.950
Ryvius.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.920
Maintaining a full 1 G-Force inside and
closely resembling earth's atmosphere...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.660
...the ship's structure is unlike any other.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.890
Its navigational system is unfamiliar.
Everything about this ship is mysterious.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.660
Ryvius.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.570
It is a place meant for us to live.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.930
It has enough food stored to feed over
one thousand people for a few months...

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.540
...and within it are 53 of the latest-model
work ships in its 38 hangers.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.440
Ryvius.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.550
Here, we must continue to live.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.210
Until the day we are rescued...

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.950
...here we are... aboard Ryvius.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.420
Infinite Ryvius

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:10.900
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.900
Although loneliness...

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:19.240
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:26.480
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.550
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.520
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:42.060
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.840
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.460
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:53.170
Some light is shed...

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.750
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:04.980
...so that we can go to a different place

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:12.990
The things I want have no shape

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:21.400
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:35.480
A Little Harmony

00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.900
Those level two guys are quite useful.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.530
At this rate, we'll be finished
one hour earlier than we planned.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.720
This place is awesome! It looks kinda
like a bridge and kinda like a laboratory.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.990
- Relative distance from Ryvius, 460.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.660
Outer wall temperature stable at 430.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:17.260
<i>That's enough, Nick.</i>

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.360
<i>Shut up! Stop nagging me!</i>

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.300
You're the one nagging us.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.230
Once we're done, let's all go and see it!

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:24.430
Sixty-seven will take overall command.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.470
Roger. Disconnecting transmitter.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.520
Operation of the emergency pod confirmed.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.380
72 hours and 50 minutes to
the L5 emergency station.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.750
Thank you!

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.590
Continue to pressure B-Group on
their inspection of the armor.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.390
Gee he talks big.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.360
<i>We entered Sere 3 without a scratch!</i>

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.350
<i>Next to this, Liebel is practically junk!</i>

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.530
- <i>What did you do that for?</i>
- <i>Learn to fly it properly!</i>

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.840
So we're stuck out here, all
because of those soldier guys.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.810
Damn!

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.200
Couldn't be.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.380
When do you think rescuers will arrive?

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.250
In a week. Two weeks at the latest.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.120
That soon?

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.520
It was in the manual, remember?
So we keep the customers calm.

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.630
Oh, right!

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:27.760
Aren't you aware that there are rescue
ships situated in designated areas?

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.000
I-Is that so?

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.300
And they did say they had been
sending rescue signals from Liebel.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.700
All we need to do now is wait.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.170
Hey! Give me a little more than this!

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:40.570
These are Zwei's instructions. A little
less for the third license control team.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.340
Are they trying to act like our instructors?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.550
We don't have much choice. It's the Zwei
guys operating this ship, after all.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:48.150
- I understand. But this is going overboard.
- It's on a rotation basis.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.180
- You'll get yours later.
- You don't have to put up with it for long.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.550
I can't see it.

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.570
Hey! Some fool just
disconnected his plug!

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.230
What? Which machine?

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.770
Um, number 47!

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.700
That's why I told you we
shouldn't have let them out there.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:10.870
Little good your advice does us now.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.210
But that 47 is good. He's flying manual,
but at 89 percent auto capabilities, and...!

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.410
34 has also plugged out.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.150
This isn't a game! Call them back!

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.890
Why not let them do as they wish?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.010
They're asking for it.

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.200
Why did you unplug us?

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.600
The guy who took off is your brother.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:36.770
What?

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.230
It looks like he did it on purpose, but
it just might be an accident, right?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:42.960
At this rate, we're gonna get lost!

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.840
At 0.01 herschels, Ryvius is in inertia.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.540
Our activity time is now less
than 6500. There's still time.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:01.110
Doesn't look like an accident, after all.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.020
Ikumi. Switch your monitor.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.260
I see. This is what he came to see.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.720
Shall we send this image to
all the internal terminals?

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:32.880
Y-Yeah.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.160
It's powerful to see, it's not
like seeing just a picture of it.

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:48.970
Incredible.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.550
Has he fallen asleep?

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.480
He must've been really nervous.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.210
Sure, being surrounded by strangers.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.360
Can you let me know more
about what you were saying?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:12.130
It appears that just before Liebel launched,
there was a submersible ship nearby.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:15.130
Also, the submersible ship detected
by the simulator is a Gestalt type...

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:18.000
...used only by the Orbital Security Bureau.

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.600
The men who attacked the bridge,
the Orbital Security Bureau...

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:27.740
...and this spaceship, we can
assume, are all linked somehow.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:30.810
- You're kidding! If that were true...!
- Linda! Hurry!

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.310
I'm coming!

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.150
Then what about our rescue?

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:37.150
Our rescue signal reaches
the whole solar system...

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:40.360
...so some place must
have got it by now.

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.790
Don't worry. Help will come.

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.560
What news on Conrad's submersible ship?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:51.700
It's been difficult to get through to them...!

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:55.570
I see. Our biggest problem in
any case, is that the Bratica...

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:58.660
...has been visible in ordinary
space for over 40 hours.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:01.180
Thanks to receiver restrictions
on the rescue signal...

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.980
...and obstruction to communication
caused by the neutrino shower...

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:07.250
...we still have about 100 hours
before the information gets out.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.320
In the meantime, our fourth fleet will
reach the target within 24 hours.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:12.950
This is not an opponent that one
group of ships can easily defeat.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:17.230
Given the fact it continues to send out
rescue signals and has hardly moved...

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:20.920
...it's highly unlikely that the people
on the ship are familiar with Bratica.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.930
They would be the Liebe Delta staff.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:25.090
We can capture them.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.870
The last thing I want is
for Shimomura to find out.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:31.030
I understand, sir.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.980
I hear the performance chart for
the Level Two guys has been posted.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.010
Let's go take a look.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.580
Looks like the top performer
is a guy called Yuki Aiba.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.150
Those marks are good enough to
pilot a high-speed spaceship.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.590
Way to go, Yuki.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.760
Do you know him?

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:47.410
Kind of.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:52.290
Why are you 10th and
me 11th, Akihiro?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:52.990
I'm sorry.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:00.090
<i>Why the hell did they have</i>
<i>to post our marks? Damn it!</i>

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:02.800
What is it?

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.840
Oh. It's nothing.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.580
How long before our next task?

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.980
About thirty minutes.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.550
Where are Nicks and Akihiro?

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.210
They're on early duty,
so they've already gone.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.450
Hello!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:15.520
Hi!

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.950
What is it, Aoi?

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.650
Ta-da!

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:21.460
What's with those clothes?

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.360
Well, we've got gravity, so why not?

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:24.330
Right?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.930
How could you react like that?

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:30.370
Sorry, sorry. You look good in it!

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:32.400
Even with my "extra weight'?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.040
Hey, did you come to show
me, or be angry with me?

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.160
I'd say both!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:38.840
Are you on your way to work?

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.240
To the dining hall again.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:42.900
If there's something you especially want,
I could make it and bring it to you.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:44.580
Don't bother.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:48.250
What?

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.920
Something happen again to upset you?

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.390
N-Nothing happened.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:59.690
Take for example delivering this food to the
ruffians. I have to do all the dirty work.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.800
But what a relief. I was a bit
nervous doing this all on my own.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.570
This is the only way we
can get over to Liebel.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.500
We're not doing this for you, you fool!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.470
H-How regrettable.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.910
His feelings have been hurt.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.140
Sorry, Charlie.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:18.880
You stay here with Criff 'till we get back.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:19.550
However!

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:20.880
Let's have some fun.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.180
S-Sure.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:28.210
I'll bet you he thinks
she's serious about him.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.890
Take your time!

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:38.700
Hey! Whaddaya say we go
after we're done here?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.900
To that place you called "awesome"?

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:43.440
Yeah. It really is awesome!

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:46.040
But we only have one hour before
our designated shower time.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.780
You can skip your shower.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.810
You realize how sweaty we are?

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.050
Let's go after we've taken a shower.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.620
Oh, Aiba!

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:54.550
Yes?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.380
You're Kouji Aiba, right?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.520
Umm... and who might you be?

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.360
I hope you're kidding, Kouji.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:02.320
I'm Juli Bahana.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.090
Of Zwei!

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:05.530
Thanks for your help before.

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:08.730
Ah, well, it was Ikumi
Oze who did everything.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:09.700
Hello.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.000
You have a younger brother, don't you?

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.170
Yes.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:17.370
Your brother didn't register with a team.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:22.080
Since your team registered late,
I added your brother to your team.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.850
You're not serious!

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.050
Should I have not...?

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:28.610
Oh, um... it's nothing.

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.620
I understand, and I'm sorry
for raising my voice.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:34.550
Please excuse me.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:38.530
So that Yuki Aiba guy who came
in first is your little brother?

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:39.860
Let's hurry and take these over.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:41.090
R-Right.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:53.900
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:58.640
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.520
Brace yourselves!

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.350
Is it really that great?

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:05.320
It looks like a warehouse.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.590
Here guys, look over here!

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:16.260
Doesn't it just blow your mind?

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.100
A simulation room?

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:20.030
No, I'd say it's something else.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.640
This isn't used to operate this ship.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:27.770
That's not all. Look closely. Ta-da!

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.580
A robot?

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:44.230
What's this? I never learned about this.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:46.930
It's too difficult to even
make out <i>what</i> it is.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:48.160
You'll get used to it!

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.370
Kreis! We've got two sets of radars!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:55.100
I told you it's difficult.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.110
That's why I'm studying it.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:59.640
Hey, will you please explain it to me?

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:04.950
Why did you post individual marks?
It'll only excite them further.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:08.580
We need discipline on the
ship until help arrives.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.990
We must recognize those with greater
abilities to assign appropriate duties.

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.920
I believe these actions are obvious
from a Captain's standpoint.

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.030
I agree with Lucson's opinion.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.260
Stein...!

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:21.100
Considering what happened
to the instructors...

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:24.130
...we're now in a position
to lead the other students.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:26.070
Please understand, Juli.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.800
I understand what you're saying, but...!

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.640
Pat! Wait!

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:34.410
Juli!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.410
Pat!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.510
Sorry. He wouldn't listen.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.450
Who's this kid?

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.080
He's one of our team members.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.050
Now, Pat. Say "Hi".

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.660
You included a boy on your team?

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.460
Come on. He's a child.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.590
But from a Captain's standpoint,
I must have you maintain morals!

00:13:55.130 --> 00:13:56.400
The radar's picking up on something!

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.430
Rescuers? Good.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.670
Charlie, get the vessel number and...!

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:01.900
Who's Charlie?

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.440
He means Good Turtleland the Third.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:05.930
He hasn't returned yet.

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:11.950
Wh-What took you so long.
I was getting worried.

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.910
Did you get along?

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.280
You could say that.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:19.750
Blood!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.720
We might've overdone things a bit.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:24.990
Not to worry. Just think of
the number of lives they took.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.260
Y-You don't mean to say...!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:31.630
No secrets behind
our backs. Got that?

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:35.000
I-I swear. I swear, so please don't shoot!

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.180
They're patrol boats. Two of them.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:43.650
Why aren't they rescue ships?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:46.580
Don't you think they're here
too soon for a rescue mission?

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:48.620
Besides, they're off the official route.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:52.890
We're just fortunate. Carabona,
contact them. Talk to them.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:56.990
R-Right. Um... Th-This is Ryvius.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:58.960
Say it correctly!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.760
W-We have escaped from the accident on
Astronaut Training Center, Liebe Delta.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:04.490
We can go home now.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:06.800
Ta-da!!

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:11.570
I had no idea you were so
gifted in baking, Faina.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:12.610
You're too kind.

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:15.800
We haven't had a treat like
this in ages, have we, Aoi?

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:17.870
Hey.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:21.220
Don't sneak up on us like that.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:22.510
What do you want, Yuki?

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.610
Where are the guys from across the hall?

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:26.410
Kouji and the others?

00:15:26.990 --> 00:15:28.180
Where the hell did they go?

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.460
A human-type robot on a spaceship.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.930
Right down to the number of legs!

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.030
Why do you laugh? Don't
you find this awesome?

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:42.340
Y-You've got great taste.

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:43.740
This is cool.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.780
I'd like to meet whoever made this thing!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.210
What a dunce!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:52.780
487 people are stranded here.
Please hurry and rescue us.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:56.450
I repeat. We have escaped from the
accident on Astronaut Training Center...!

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:57.490
Haven't they responded yet?

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:59.120
Lucson! We can't even
connect online with them!

00:15:59.120 --> 00:15:59.780
What?

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.830
The patrol boats have just released
something! About 600 of them!

00:16:04.830 --> 00:16:05.730
Missiles?

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.830
You're kidding.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:10.230
There's no possibility of
that. Let me analyze it.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:14.300
Now, shall we start from the
beginning, and cut the cake?

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:17.270
Wait. The jasmine tea's not ready yet!

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:21.410
Hurry! Hurry! Hurry! Hurry!
Hurry! Hurry! Hurry...!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:24.070
<i>Maybe I shouldn't have told him.</i>

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.880
What's that?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.290
They've attached to us!

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:41.960
This appears to be a capture.

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.900
Yes. For emergency transport.

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:47.900
We're saved. They're gonna
transport the whole ship.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:51.510
But something's not right. Normally, they
would establish contact with us first.

00:16:51.510 --> 00:16:54.960
You mean, these guys are the same as
the guys that attacked the bridge?

00:16:56.980 --> 00:16:59.580
Where is the cockpit to this thing?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.620
You're gonna hurt yourself, Nicks.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.450
Looks like these are the controls.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.480
To move the robot?

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:07.860
You sure you're allowed to touch that?

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.350
I don't see why not!

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:14.030
What is it?

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:16.000
Kouji!

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:22.200
That guy.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:27.070
Why the hell am I on your team?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.640
I never asked you for the favor!

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.380
What was that?

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:37.940
There must be guys working on the outside.

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.360
<i>Capture complete.</i>

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.090
<i>There is no reaction by the target.</i>

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:47.130
Commence transfer.

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:48.030
Commence transfer.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:51.730
L-Let go!

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:55.370
Seeing you smile makes me sick.
Stop making a fool of me.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.700
What are you talking about?

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:59.040
Stop acting like my guardian,
doing things behind my back!

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:00.780
It wasn't me who did it!

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:01.810
You could've said "no"!

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:05.010
Don't blame me! It's your fault
for not registering with any team!

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:06.310
Stop it!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.280
Get outta my way!

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:11.090
What should we do?

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.280
Let them do as they wish.

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:15.460
What do you mean? They're
here to rescue us, right?

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:17.250
We can't be positive! This is too risky!

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:20.660
Damn you!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.750
Even if they do capture
us, they'll save us.

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:24.860
Why?

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.470
In spite of being younger than me!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:30.240
Not that again!

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:32.270
What'll we do if they're also killers?

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:34.540
But they could be rescuers!

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:36.510
Aren't you afraid?

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:44.490
I don't wanna be killed.

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:49.180
But we have no choice. We don't fully
understand this navigation system.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:50.420
Heiger!

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:51.960
We don't have time.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.300
At this rate, we're being
captured by the patrol ship.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.260
How dare you!

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.800
Do you want to die?

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:05.970
No! I don't wanna just sit
here, waiting to be killed!

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:08.970
Don't you want to live?

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.520
Damn you!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.520
<i>Why?</i>

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.960
<i>Why does this have to happen?</i>

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:23.920
<i>Damn!</i>

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.230
<i>Damn!</i>

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.360
<i>Get real!</i>

00:19:27.360 --> 00:19:29.520
<i>What is it, anyway?</i>

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:32.370
<i>What did I do to deserve this?</i>

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:37.500
You're an eyesore.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.240
Huh? It's not... a radar?

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:45.410
The navigation system has been
activated. Output levels rising!

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:26.890
What's going on?

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.390
Gravitational waves confirmed!

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:31.990
The field is spreading,
with the target in its core!

00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:33.290
A trap?

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.730
Abend one and two are being
drawn into the field!

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:36.700
What?

00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:48.440
Th-The boat...!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.640
We've lost our target.
It's entered the Geduld.

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:17.710
How much time before the burst?

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:19.470
Six hours, twelve minutes!

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:21.240
We're switching to plan Y!

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:22.370
Yes, sir!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.570
Aiba: Ritsuko, Kouji and Yuki

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:29.080
<i>7:00 p.m. Standard Time on the 13th...</i>

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:33.020
<i>...due to a malfunction at the</i>
<i>Astronaut License Training Center...</i>

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:35.250
<i>...Liebe Delta has fallen into the</i>
<i>Geduld, and has been crushed.</i>

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:37.960
<i>We have not yet received full details...</i>

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:41.790
<i>...but there is little chance that any</i>
<i>students or staff on board have survived.</i>

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:48.600
<i>Right now, patrol boats from the Orbital</i>
<i>Security Bureau are heading to the scene.</i>

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:50.570
<i>We will update you after the burst.</i>

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:55.970
Due to the effect of neutrino,
we will now be signing off the air.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.680
So they're concealing their actions.

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:00.650
It appears that they're after Ryvius.

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:04.980
I won't allow that. That's our last resort!

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:11.880
In your dry eyes...

00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:16.950
...a silhouette appears

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:21.660
The blue colored future...

00:22:21.660 --> 00:22:27.750
...swayed and glittered

00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:37.810
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:46.410
...freedom out of pity

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:54.860
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:58.760
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:05.130
goodbye

00:23:09.190 --> 00:23:10.920
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:14.530
Next episode: My Moment
At a depth of Sere 2, Ryvius
was under enemy attack.

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.960
Next episode: My Moment
Enemy? That's right, we have enemies.

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:18.960
Next episode: My Moment
But why? For what purpose?

00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:22.740
Next episode: My Moment
While forced to keep these many thoughts
closed within ourselves, we remain active.

00:23:22.740 --> 00:23:26.210
Next episode: My Moment
Among the twinkling flashes, the
second hand of fate is set into motion.

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:29.400
Next episode; My Moment
That moment... My moment...
